2.41.0

From 3bdba2ae2ed1158b9fc9822562d86b8e287d8490 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:48:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] virtio-gpu: don't stall the control queue behind a blob
 unmap

Unmapping a hostmem blob detaches its MemoryRegion, and the virgl mapping
has to survive until that MR is fully unreferenced (a flat view may still
be under an RCU reader), which takes ~100 ms.  Blocking all command
processing for that grace period, as before, serialized a burst of unmaps
into multi-second round trips for every other command: a D3D12 guest
tearing down hundreds of staging heaps pushed unrelated packets past
dxgkrnl's timeout, and the app died with DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_RESET.

Keep the queue flowing instead.  UNMAP_BLOB is answered as soon as the
subregion is gone -- the guest cannot reach the pages any more -- and the
virgl unmap runs from the resume BH once the region finalizes.  Only work
that needs that unmap to have happened waits for it, and per resource
rather than per queue: an UNREF of a still-mapped resource is completed
(virgl unref + response) from the same BH, leaving the queue meanwhile
(cmd->deferred), and a re-MAP of a resource whose previous mapping is
still going away is the one case that still suspends the queue.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
