From bb76def9a79d81b99c430905d1f9debd20393645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:39:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] edid: set the established timings III bit of every mode that
 has one

edid_fill_modes() puts a mode in one of the eight standard timing slots
while there are free ones, and sets the mode's bit in the Established
Timings III descriptor only once the slots are used up. Which modes end
up where depends on their order in the table: with no size limit,
1920x1200, 1600x1200, 1680x1050, 1440x900, 1280x1024 and 1280x960 get a
standard timing and no bit.

A guest that builds its mode list from the established timings and does
not read the standard timings never offers those modes. The QemuVga
driver that Mac OS 9 and Mac OS X use on mac99 is one: it reads the
established timings, the Established Timings III descriptor and the
CTA-861 video data block.

Set the bit whenever the mode has one, next to the standard timing. The
bits are the ones VESA defines for these modes at 60 Hz, and the modes
were advertised before, so a guest that reads both sees the same list.

Based on a change by giovariot.

