From 1219f88549f6dc89466bc30012fe91068f8cf44a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Guyette <joshguyette@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:06:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] accel/hvf, os-posix: support -overcommit mem-lock=on on macOS

mlockall() returns ENOSYS on macOS, so -overcommit mem-lock=on failed at
startup. Lock each guest RAM mapping with mlock() as HVF maps it instead,
and let os_mlock() succeed on macOS.

On a 2017 Intel MacBook Pro (16 GB) with an 8 GB Windows 11 guest, about
8 GB stays wired with the option on. Without it, a memory-heavy run on our
earlier fork left only 2.8 GB resident. On utm-edition I measured no idle
