Subject: [PATCH] screamer: pace TX DMA to the sample rate

With 1 GB or more RAM Mac OS 9 turns VM off and its sound driver uses a
single 4 KiB ring. Screamer consumed the whole ring at once, so the
driver saw both half-buffer interrupts before anything played and kept
restarting: alert sounds came out as short blips.

Complete OUTPUT commands at the codec sample rate instead, with a small
FIFO lead, and count FRAME_CNT as frames are consumed.

