  memory, as real DBDMA does. Since only res_count/xfer_status are written
  back now, the Mac OS 9 Screamer driver (VM off, >= 1 GB) never saw the
  frame counter it samples with LOAD_WORD.
- dbdma_control_write: honour the software-settable device status bits
  s0-s7. The Mac OS 9 sound input driver sets s0 to make its INPUT command
  branch out of the ring; it was ignored, so the ring never stopped.
