TX and RX transfers now stay in flight on a timer, which exposed a few
paths that assumed they complete at once:

- A zero-length INPUT descriptor never completed: the RX timer returned
  early on len == 0, so the channel stayed "processing" forever.
- mac_dbdma_reset left io.processing set while screamer_reset deleted the
  timers that would clear it, so sound stayed dead after a guest reboot
  that interrupted playback or recording.
- tx_flush cleared io.processing on PAUSE or FLUSH too, so DBDMA restarted
  the descriptor still being paced and its frames were sent twice. Only
  clear it when the guest stops the channel, as rx_flush does.
- If the virtual clock went backwards (loadvm), TX got no credit until
  it caught up again.

Also factor the duplicated res_count/xfer_status write-back and the
"guest cleared RUN" test into helpers, and fix a block comment style.

