From 80d3e749a83f836b724a17f880446d3876e315d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Guyette <joshguyette@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:30:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] audio: steadier HDA playback on a busy Mac

Three changes, based on OmacVM's patches (MIT,
github.com/gillesgoetsch/OmacVM, PR #93):

- system/main.c: on macOS the main loop thread asks for user-interactive
  QoS. It feeds the HDA DMA timer and the audio timer and runs virgl; at
  the default QoS it waits behind the vCPU threads, so the sound breaks up.
  QEMU_MAIN_LOOP_QOS=default keeps the old behaviour.
- hda-codec: on a full output ring, keep the queued samples and only reset
  the catch-up debt, instead of dropping the whole 8 KB buffer (~42 ms).
- hda-codec: pacing (new "pace" property, on by default). After a stalled
  main loop, take the guest's audio at most 1/32 faster than real time
  instead of all at once.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Josh Guyette <joshguyette@yahoo.com>
---
