From 0f1b8666d16024fc1a615ef641833ceebc260039 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Miller <emkey1@oneopa.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] migration/savevm: answer the command that starts a snapshot
 job first

snapshot-save, snapshot-load and snapshot-delete start a job whose
coroutine schedules the actual work as a bottom half in the main
AioContext and yields. The command itself runs in a bottom half of the
iohandler context, and its reply is sent by the QMP dispatcher
coroutine, which is woken through that same context once the command
handler returns. The main loop gets to the main AioContext's bottom
half before it gets back to the dispatcher, and the work blocks the
main loop until it is done. So the reply goes out only after the
snapshot has been written or loaded, together with the job's
"concluded" event.

A client that puts a deadline on the reply (QEMUKit, used by UTM, waits
10 s) then reports a save that takes longer as failed, although QEMU
finishes it and the state stays in the image with nothing referring to
it.

Put the work behind the reply: the job coroutine now schedules a bottom
half in the iohandler context, and that one schedules the work in the
main AioContext. It runs in the same pass over the iohandler context as
the dispatcher's wake-up, and the main AioContext is only dispatched
after that pass, so the reply is written first. Errors are reported
through the job as before.

Measured over QMP with an aarch64 HVF guest holding 2 GiB of random data
in tmpfs (2.7 GiB vmstate), time from sending the command to its reply /
to JOB_STATUS_CHANGE "concluded":

                    before                  after
  snapshot-save     1467.4 ms / 1467.5 ms   0.9 ms / 1467.6 ms
  snapshot-load     1433.5 ms / 1433.6 ms   1.3 ms / 1425.4 ms
  snapshot-delete     90.3 ms /   90.3 ms   1.7 ms /   91.6 ms

Upstream QEMU master (v11.2.0-rc0) schedules the work the same way and
has the same ordering.

(cherry picked from commit 3f572363b83a3b64de9fd2d21a5fbbfc652caff8
 of https://github.com/emkey1/qemu; commit message rewritten)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-2
---
